--
found no match
--
A class template with a template-template parameter used as its BASE
CLASS (`struct buft : _Layout<_Tp, _Alloc, buft<...>>`), where the
bound template lives inside a (nested inline) namespace, and the base's
members are imported by using-declaration and called through a nested
class's parent pointer -- libc++'s
__split_buffer/__split_buffer_pointer_layout/_ConstructTransaction
shape.  The TT-param binding must resolve to the namespace-nested
template at the use site (N5008 [temp.param]/1, [temp.names]/2); a
failure here silently drops the base and the using-declared overload
set, and the assertion becomes vacuous (hence it is pinned).
